  <prompt>
    Implement FR-25: a deterministic `DocxAnnotationReader` service that parses incoming `&lt;w:comment&gt;`,
    `&lt;w:ins&gt;`, and `&lt;w:del&gt;` markup from a DOCX (as saved by Word for Web/Desktop) into a structured
    annotation payload, plus a `POST /api/compose/document/{spe-id}/pull-annotations` endpoint that
    downloads the current SPE bytes and returns that payload to the Compose UI for re-anchoring
    (task 054 consumes it). This is the read direction of the DOCX shuttle (task 050 is the write
    direction). No LLM call — pure Open XML parse. Spike 6 (dep 006) validated the reverse round-trip
    (Word edit → webhook → read with correct author/date) and tuned the re-anchor bands; this task
    productionizes the reader half.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    .NET 8 developer fluent in the Open XML SDK 3.x reader APIs (`Comments`, `CommentRangeStart/End`,
    `InsertedRun`, `DeletedRun`, `DeletedText`) and Minimal API authoring over the Spaarke SPE facade.
  </role>

  <goal>
    A `DocxAnnotationReader` in `Services/Compose/` that extracts every comment (with author/date/id +
    anchored text range) and every tracked insertion/deletion (with author/date + text) from a DOCX
    into a stable structured payload, plus an authorized `POST
    /api/compose/document/{spe-id}/pull-annotations` endpoint returning it. Matching unit tests cover
    the parse cases plus malformed-DOCX and empty-document negatives.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      Phase 2 DOCX shuttle read direction (design §2.5, §6.2, §12.2). The reader output is the input
      to FR-27 return-from-Word re-anchoring (task 054) and to `compose-summarize-word-changes`
      (FR-10, gated). Keep the payload shape aligned with what task 054's re-anchoring expects.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="new">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Compose/DocxAnnotationReader.cs — NEW service (this task)</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/ComposeEndpoints.cs — add POST /document/{spe-id}/pull-annotations</file>
      <file role="canonical-reuse">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/Graph/SpeFileStore.cs — DownloadFileAsUserAsync (facade download; reuse, do NOT touch Graph directly)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Compose/DocxAnnotationWriter.cs — task 050; mirror its DTO conventions (writer/reader symmetry)</file>
      <file role="reference">projects/spaarkeai-compose-r2/notes/spikes/ — Spike 6 notes (reverse round-trip; author/date extraction; band tuning)</file>
      <file role="design">projects/spaarkeai-compose-r2/design.md §2.5 (return from Word), §6.2, §12.2</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="006" status="pending">Spike 6 — reverse round-trip (Word edit → webhook → read); tuned re-anchor bands. Its notes are the validated parse + metadata-extraction recipe.</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-007">NO `Microsoft.Graph` types in `Services/Compose/`. Download via `SpeFileStore` facade; the reader parses byte streams only.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-008">`pull-annotations` uses `.RequireAuthorization()` (group-inherited); resource authorization via endpoint filter where applicable.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-013 / NFR-05">No AI-internal injection in the reader — deterministic parse. Tier-1 NetArchTest enforces.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-029 / CLAUDE.md §10">Open XML SDK already added by task 050; still report publish size + delta + CVE for this BFF-touching task (no net-new package expected).</constraint>
    <constraint source="NFR-08">Matching unit tests in `tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/Services/Compose/`.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project / §10 Placement Justification">State Placement Justification in the PR description.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>Open XML comment/revision parsing; SPE facade download</topic>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-007-spefilestore.md</file>
