  <justification>
    <existing>No existing service parses OOXML annotations. `DocxAnnotationWriter` (050) is the write direction; the platform `ITextExtractor` extracts plain text, not comment/revision structure. No overlap.</existing>
    <extension>Distinct read responsibility, symmetric to the writer; separate unit-tested unit keeps each direction independently verifiable. Reuses `ComposeEndpoints.cs` + `SpeFileStore` — no new plumbing.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Without it, a Word-added comment/track-change cannot round-trip back — FR-25 acceptance ("a Word-added comment + track-change round-trips back with correct author/date") fails, and FR-27 re-anchoring (task 054) has no input to re-anchor.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <acceptance-criteria testable="true">
    <criterion testable="true">A Word-authored comment parses back with correct author, date, id, and anchored text range.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Tracked insertions and deletions parse with correct type, author, date, and text.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`POST /api/compose/document/{spe-id}/pull-annotations` requires authorization and returns the structured payload from current SPE bytes.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: an empty (no-annotation) document returns an empty payload, not an error.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: a malformed/non-DOCX input returns 400 ProblemDetails.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">No `Microsoft.Graph` type in `Services/Compose/`; no AI-internal injection (NetArchTest green).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Matching unit tests pass; BFF build green; publish-size + CVE reported.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <execution>
    <skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill>
  </execution>

  <notes>
    Completed 2026-07-09. NEW `DocxAnnotationReader` (Services/Compose/) parses w:comment +
    CommentRangeStart/End (author/date/id/commentText/anchorText/paragraphHint, multi-paragraph
    anchor walk per Spike 6 EDGE-R4) and w:ins/w:del (author/date/text via DeletedText not Text
    per EDGE-R1; w:date normalized to UTC per EDGE-R2). Pure byte[]->record transform, zero I/O,
    zero AI reach, zero new package (DocumentFormat.OpenXml already a dep since task 050).
    Instantiated directly in ComposeEndpoints.cs (not DI-registered) to keep this task's footprint
    to exactly: NEW DocxAnnotationReader.cs, MODIFIED ComposeEndpoints.cs (route addition only,
    existing routes preserved), NEW DocxAnnotationReaderTests.cs (9 tests) — no edits to
    IComposeService/ComposeService/ComposeModule.cs, honoring the shared-worktree write boundary.
    New `POST /api/compose/document/{documentSpeId}/pull-annotations` downloads current SPE bytes
    via ISpeFileOperations facade (ADR-007), parses via the reader, returns structured
    comments+revisions; RequireAuthorization() inherited from the group (ADR-008); malformed DOCX
    -> 400 ProblemDetails, empty document -> empty payload (200), SPE 404 -> 404, OBO denial ->
    403. Build: 0 errors. Tests: 9/9 new, 224/224 Compose suite green. ADR-013 Compose facade
    architecture test: 2/2 green (no AI-internal injection). ADR-007 Graph-isolation architecture
    test has 1 PRE-EXISTING failure in unrelated files (Services/Communication/*,
    Infrastructure/Errors/ProblemDetailsHelper.cs, Api/Office/Errors/OfficeProblemDetail.cs) —
    confirmed via git status these files were not touched by this task. Publish size: 49.75 MB
    compressed incl. PDBs (baseline 49.63 MB, delta +0.12 MB — negligible, no new package).
    `dotnet list package --vulnerable --include-transitive`: 1 pre-existing HIGH
    (Microsoft.Kiota.Abstractions, transitive via Microsoft.Graph) — zero new packages added by
    this task, csproj untouched.
  </notes>
</task>
